his explains why row 3 in the test case remains all zeros.\n\n**Confirming No Wrap-Around**\n\nI've thoroughly checked for diagonal neighbors, and it's clear there's no wrap-around logic at play with the grid boundaries. This means cells outside the defined bounds will simply remain 0, as observed in the training data's column 3.\n\n",
